Account Creation on Policy Issuance
What Happens When a Policy is Issued?
1.	Bill Account Creation
•	As soon as the policy is officially issued, the system creates a billing account
•	This account will track all billing-related activities for that policy.
2.	Receivable Amount Posted
•	The premium amount that the customer needs to pay is recorded in this billing account.
•	Think of it like: Adding the amount due to the account so the system knows what to collect.
3.	Policy Linked to Bill Account
•	The issued policy is connected to the billing account.
•	Why important: This link ensures that payments are correctly applied to the right policy.
Key Points to Remember
•	Billing Account = Central place for all payment tracking for a policy.
•	Receivable Amount = Premium due recorded in the account.
•	Linking Policy to Billing Account = Ensures accurate billing and reporting.
